  "correctValue": "74",
  "solution": {
    "text": "If given line makes an isosceles triangle with the planes, then the angle that the line makes with the normal vectors to the planes are equal<br />A vector parallel to the line is <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math><br />A normal vector to the first plane <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1,3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math><br />A normal vector to the second&nbsp;plane <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>b</mi> <mo>→</mo> </mover> <mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub> <mi>n</mi> <mi>i</mi> </msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>b</mi> <mo>→</mo> </mover> </mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"> <mrow> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub> <mi>n</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>b</mi> <mo>→</mo> </mover> <mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub> <mi>n</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mi>b</mi> <mo>→</mo> </mover> </mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"> <mrow> <mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub> <mi>n</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </mfrac> <mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo